<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (GPT-5.6 Sol)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol";
    dc:identifier "gpt-5.6-sol-medium".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch06-22--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch06-22: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.64";
    dc:description "Known class 4 systems have public, provably persistent structures, so many instances are resolvable. The universal necessity is close to a definitional intuition and cannot be established over an informal class by available data alone.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/mixed";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Define a persistent structure as a finite-support or periodic-background pattern whose identity survives indefinitely, then search and prove persistence for every rule in a specified class 4 catalog. A class 4 rule with a proof that all finite structures die would refute the universal claim.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Class 4 lacks a formal exhaustive definition.", "Finite simulation cannot prove indefinite persistence.", "Structure identity depends on background and equivalence choices.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.67"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch06-22--gpt--dataset-1>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.638"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
